# .trivyignore: exceptions for `trivy config .`, with the reason for each.
#
# We can't fix these without breaking the workloads. Each one is explained
# below and kept contained by namespace + NetworkPolicy (and PVCs where the
# workload is stateful). Trivy reads the check IDs listed here, one per line.

# Traefik needs to read the TLS certificate secrets (get/list/watch only).
KSV-0041

# Stateful LAMP and DB workloads write to their root filesystem (apache web
# root, Galera SST/recovery, OpenSearch config/logs, Keycloak data), so
# readOnlyRootFilesystem would break them. The data lives on PVCs, behind a
# namespace and a NetworkPolicy.
KSV-0014

# blackbox-exporter needs NET_RAW to send ICMP probes.
KSV-0119

# node-exporter reads node metrics, so it needs the host network, host PID,
# host port and read-only host root mounts.
KSV-0009
KSV-0010
KSV-0024
KSV-0121

# Prometheus needs nodes/proxy to scrape kubelet and cAdvisor.
KSV-0047

# Wazuh indexer (OpenSearch) needs a privileged init container to set
# vm.max_map_count=262144.
KSV-0017

# The LDAP-sync CronJobs run kubectl exec into the app pod to call the app CLI
# (an import that is safe to run again).
KSV-0053

# The "secret" in the privacyIDEA radius config and the Dolibarr OIDC PHP is a
# template variable / source code, not a stored credential.
KSV-0109
